"""ICD-10-CM description vocabulary — GENERATED by tools/mine_icd_vocab.py.

Every lowercase word in the ICD-10-CM code descriptions, chapters A-T
(CMS, public domain; V-Y external-cause chapters excluded), minus:
  - any word that is a personal name in inkguard/name_registry.py, a
    2000 US Census surname or a 1990 US Census first name (a surname
    must never become "clinical");
  - any word the existing lexicon files as an ambiguous eponym;
  - any word that ICD itself capitalizes mid-description (eponyms,
    genera, places);
  - general-English words at zipf >= 4.0 (common enough to be a surname
    somewhere, and already handled by the frequency layer).

What is left is organ, structure, lesion and procedure vocabulary —
"urethra", "cystocele", "scrotum" — the words real operative notes open
sentences with and that the name layers kept mistaking for surnames.

The data is in inkguard/data/lexicon_icd_vocab.json.gz, written by tools/mine_icd_vocab.py
through inkguard._data.pack_module. Do not edit by hand."""
from inkguard._data import load as _load

_D = _load('lexicon_icd_vocab')
ICD_VOCAB: frozenset = _D['ICD_VOCAB']
del _D
